{
  "_provenance": {
    "what": "A POST /air/offer_requests response, JFK-LHR, one adult, 2026-11-12.",
    "captured": false,
    "how": "SYNTHESISED, but not guessed: the field names and nesting are taken from Duffel's own Python SDK (duffel-api 0.6.2, duffel_api/models/offer.py), which is the authoritative parser for this payload. No Duffel credential was available on the machine this was written on, so no value here was observed.",
    "therefore": "It proves the adapter reads the schema the SDK parses. Replace it with a real capture from a duffel_test_ token and re-run the adapter tests; a field that moved shows up as a dropped itinerary, not as silence.",
    "note_on_test_mode": "A real duffel_test_ token returns the fictional carrier Duffel Airways (ZZ) with invented prices, NOT the carriers below. Offer off_zz_testmode is included so the adapter's behaviour on an uncurated carrier is exercised, because that is the first thing a new token actually shows you.",
    "exercises": [
      "operating_carrier equal to marketing_carrier, which Duffel always states rather than omitting",
      "a codeshare where they differ",
      "a fare_brand_name with no checked bag, and the same flight on a brand that includes one",
      "available_services carrying a REAL price for an extra checked bag",
      "a segment with aircraft: null, which must abstain",
      "a two-segment connection on one offer, so bags are through-checked",
      "an uncurated carrier (ZZ), which keeps the option but drops the carrier rating",
      "an itinerary through an uncurated airport, which must be dropped rather than guessed",
      "an airport whose feed time_zone disagrees with the curated zone table"
    ]
  },
